        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-12-26T11:57:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Not sure about that situation, but I have had turns like that with some plus to damage on the team. Overdo it playing For the Greater Good can often deal 15+ damage before your play phase. Either play Primed Punhc, use the power, then deal 4 more damge, since it is the start of the turn still. With +3 damage, that's 4+4+7=15. Nice start of the turn. Playing Battlefield Experience using the power, then playing Amplified Combat with the destruction clause with +3 can deal 5+5+4+4=18 damage. I have done both in-game, not to Iron Legacy, just in general. Then just go all out during your play phase and power phase, and the damage can really get up there.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
