      {
        "id": 187500,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-12-28T22:09:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, my favorite thing about KNYFE is combos. She can play 3 or more cards, use multiple powers dealing multiple instances of damage, without too much trouble.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, like was said, she really likes going toe-to-toe with the highest hp villain. She can reduce their damage, increase her own, and then go to town hitting them an average of 4 times a turn if not more.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Or, with her one-shots and the blade and gauntlet, she can handle multi-target situations really well, destroying or at least brutally weakening multiple minions, while still hitting the big target.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Oh... and don't use Wrecking Uppercut against the Ennead... I found out that was a bad idea the hard way.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:13:18.485Z",
