      {
        "id": 187503,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-03T16:39:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"robb8888\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> robb8888:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One of my biases against KNYFE may come from the fact that for whatever reason, I found myself playing her against Spite numerous times, with no buffing or damage-redirecting heroes to help. &nbsp;Between Spite's DR, KNYFE's lack of DR (which made the \"take damage whenever you use a power\" really problematic), and the continuous ongoing/equipment destruction (so she never got to keep her Blade/Gauntlet/anything else in play very long), she just wasn't doing much good, and was leaking HP like a sieve. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This is why I always bring Legacy(for tanking and evolving vs the toxic damage)&nbsp;and Wraith(to reduce everything else Donovan throws)&nbsp;along if I can when I fight Spite. Especially when I have Inspiring Presence as the card that always comes back into play.</p>",
