        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-10T11:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Thanks for all of the tips! &nbsp;I've been having more success with KNYFE lately. &nbsp;Based on the above, I'm now using her as sort of a kamikaze cannon: &nbsp;I basically assume that she's going to get incapped 50% of the time, so I take any early opportunity I can to buff her damage, don't care a fig about her HP (since her incap powers are great) &nbsp;and just use her to pound on the main bad guy mercilessly, stopping every so often to skip-skip if she doesn't have any great one-shots in hand, or if they won't do above-average damage (e.g., I usually won't bother playing an un-buffed Incidental Contact or Amplified Combatant unless even their unbuffed damage is sufficient to take out some crucial targets.). &nbsp;I think KNYFE is the only hero I use as sort of a \"consumable resource\"; every other hero I try to keep alive as long as possible. &nbsp;KNYFE is more like putting a car's accelerator all the way to the floor and going head-on full speed until the fuel runs out.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:13:18.736Z",
